course: dictionary
lesson: 16108
title: A Welshman, a Welshwoman, the Welsh
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A Welshman is a man or boy from Wales. Wales is a country in the west of Great Britain, and it is part of the United Kingdom. «Owen is a Welshman from a small town in Wales.» The clue is in the word itself: Welsh tells you the country, and man tells you it is a male person.
explain: A woman from Wales is a Welshwoman. More than one man is Welshmen, not Welshmans. «Sarah is a Welshwoman, and her two cousins are Welshmen.» When you talk about all the people of Wales together, you can say the Welsh or Welsh people.
explain: Words about people from a country often start with a capital letter. Welshman, Welshwoman and Welsh all begin with a capital W. Look at the words around it in a sentence: «The Welshmen cheered loudly when their team scored.» The cheering and the team tell you this is about sport.
fact: A Welshman is a man or boy from Wales.
fact: A Welshwoman is a woman from Wales.
fact: The plural of Welshman is Welshmen.
fact: Wales is a country in the west of Great Britain, and it is part of the United Kingdom.
fact: Many Welsh people speak Welsh, called Cymraeg, as well as English.
exercise: «Owen is a Welshman from a small town in Wales.» Where is Owen from? | Ireland | *Wales | Scotland | England
exercise: What is the plural of Welshman? | Welshmans | Welshmens | *Welshmen | Welshmanes
exercise: What is a Welshwoman? | A language spoken in Wales | A woman from Scotland | A man from Wales | *A woman from Wales
test: What do we call all the people of Wales together? | *The Welsh | Irish | Scots | English
test: Many Welsh people speak which language as well as English? | *Welsh, called Cymraeg | Gaelic | French | Spanish
exam: Which word means a woman from Wales? | *Welshwoman | Irishwoman | Scotswoman | Welshman
